<title>ITALY: Italy's Deroma H1 1996 profit and turnover rises.</title>
<headline>Italy's Deroma H1 1996 profit and turnover rises.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Deroma Holding, which describes itself as the world's leading maker of terracotta pots and vases, said it posted first half 1996 net profit of 9.3 billion lire against a previous 8.3 billion, on consolidated turnover of 75.3 billion lire against 71.4 billion.</p>
<p>The company, which hopes to be listed on the Milan stock exchange in early 1997, said in a statement its first half cash flow was 7.5 billion lire or equal to 10 percent of turnover, 81 percent of which came from abroad.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
